    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! All 28 tests are passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**1. `src/finetune/index.js`** \u2014 Added named exports for constants\n   - The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available via the default export\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n**2. `src/eval/metrics.js`** \u2014 Fixed `toxicityMetric` function signature\n   - The function was accepting an optional `bannedTerms` parameter\n   - When called from `runEvaluations` with `(outputs, references)`, the references array was being treated as banned terms\n   - This caused all outputs to be flagged as toxic even when they contained no actual banned words\n   - Changed the function to only accept `outputs` and always use the default banned terms\n\nAll 28 tests now pass successfully. The changes maintain backward compatibility for public exports and properly fix the intended behavior as defined by the tests.",
